<section class="snap-section faq" id="faq">
  <div class="faq-layout">
    <header class="faq-intro">
      <p class="eyebrow">FAQ</p>
      <h2>Questions, answered with the same care as the models.</h2>
    </header>
    <div class="faq-list">
      <article class="faq-item is-open">
        <button class="faq-q" type="button" aria-expanded="true">
          <span>What is Maint-IQ?</span>
          <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        </button>
        <p class="faq-a">
          Maint-IQ is a predictive-maintenance analytics platform that uses machine learning
          to analyse bearing-vibration data, identify anomalous behaviour, assess potential
          failure risk, and help interpret the factors behind its predictions.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-q" type="button" aria-expanded="false">
          <span>How does Maint-IQ identify potential equipment failures?</span>
          <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        </button>
        <p class="faq-a">
          Maint-IQ processes vibration-derived features and applies machine-learning techniques
          to identify unusual patterns and estimate failure risk. Its analytical approach
          combines anomaly detection, failure prediction, and model explainability to support
          further investigation.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-q" type="button" aria-expanded="false">
          <span>What kind of data does Maint-IQ analyse?</span>
          <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        </button>
        <p class="faq-a">
          The current project focuses on bearing-vibration datasets. These signals can be
          transformed into time-domain and frequency-domain features that help
          machine-learning models identify changes in equipment behaviour.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-q" type="button" aria-expanded="false">
          <span>Can Maint-IQ explain why a prediction was made?</span>
          <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        </button>
        <p class="faq-a">
          Yes. On the analytics page, Explain opens a concise reading of the selected graph
          using the plotted values, thresholds, and model outputs so findings can be
          investigated rather than treated as unexplained decisions.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-q" type="button" aria-expanded="false">
          <span>How reliable are Maint-IQ's predictions?</span>
          <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        </button>
        <p class="faq-a">
          Reliability depends on the quality and coverage of the available data, the model,
          and the operating conditions represented in the dataset. Maint-IQ's models should be
          evaluated using held-out test data and metrics such as precision, recall, F1 score,
          and false-positive rate. Predictions should be treated as decision-support
          information, not guarantees.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-q" type="button" aria-expanded="false">
          <span>Can Maint-IQ monitor industrial equipment in real time?</span>
          <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        </button>
        <p class="faq-a">
          Maint-IQ currently analyses prepared bearing datasets from uploaded or historical
          sources. Live sensor ingestion for continuous real-time monitoring is planned for a
          later release.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-q" type="button" aria-expanded="false">
          <span>Can Maint-IQ estimate a machine's remaining useful life?</span>
          <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        </button>
        <p class="faq-a">
          Remaining useful life (RUL) estimation aims to estimate how much operating life a
          component may have left before reaching a defined failure threshold. This
          capability depends on suitable degradation data and validation. Any experimental
          RUL estimates should be interpreted cautiously, not as guaranteed maintenance
          deadlines.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
